---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import CTA from "../components/CTA.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Navigate Delhi | Delhi Concierge">
    <!-- HERO -->

    <section class="hero section">
        <div class="container hero-wrapper">
            <div>
                <span
                    style="text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:2px;font-size:.8rem;color:#777;font-weight:600"
                >
                    Welcome to the capital
                </span>

                <h1>Navigating Delhi Without the Chaos</h1>

                <p>
                    Delhi can feel intense at first. Traffic, crowds, different
                    social norms, and endless choices can create
                    <strong>sensory overload</strong> for newcomers.
                </p>

                <p>
                    But with the right perspective and local insight, the city
                    begins to make sense. What once felt overwhelming becomes
                    surprisingly enjoyable.
                </p>

                <a href="/blog" class="btn" style="margin-top:1.5rem">
                    Explore Practical Guides
                </a>
            </div>

            <div>
                <img
                    src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1587474260584-136574528ed5?auto=format&fit=crop&q=80&w=800"
                    class="main-img"
                    alt="Delhi city architecture"
                />
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- KNOWLEDGE SECTION -->

    <section class="section guide-section">
        <div class="container guide-container">
            <h2 class="guide-title">Understanding How Delhi Moves</h2>

            <p class="guide-intro">
                Delhi begins to make sense once you understand its rhythms.
                Transport, neighbourhood culture and daily logistics follow
                patterns that locals intuitively know. Learning these patterns
                removes a lot of the friction that newcomers often experience.
            </p>

            <!-- TRANSPORT PANEL -->

            <div class="guide-panel">
                <div class="panel-header">
                    <svg class="panel-icon" viewBox="0 0 64 64">
                        <circle cx="32" cy="32" r="26"></circle>
                        <path d="M18 34h28M24 24h16"></path>
                    </svg>

                    <div>
                        <h3>Transportation in Delhi</h3>
                        <p>
                            Choosing the right transport depends on distance,
                            timing and comfort.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="accordion">
                    <details open>
                        <summary>Delhi Metro</summary>

                        <p>
                            If you want the most predictable way to move across
                            Delhi, the Metro is it. It bypasses traffic entirely
                            and connects most major parts of the city — South
                            Delhi, Connaught Place, Old Delhi, Gurgaon and
                            Noida.
                        </p>

                        <p>
                            Stations are clean, announcements are in English,
                            and trains run frequently. For many expats the Metro
                            becomes the easiest option for longer journeys
                            across the city.
                        </p>

                        <p>
                            Rush hours can be crowded, especially around 9am and
                            6pm. Outside those times it’s surprisingly
                            comfortable and often faster than driving.
                        </p>
                    </details>

                    <details>
                        <summary>Uber & Ride Apps</summary>

                        <p>
                            Ride-hailing apps like Uber and Ola are the simplest
                            option for most newcomers. They remove the need to
                            negotiate fares and navigation works reliably across
                            most parts of the city.
                        </p>

                        <p>
                            Cars are widely available, especially in South Delhi
                            and central districts. Travel times can vary
                            depending on traffic, so short distances may take
                            longer during peak hours.
                        </p>

                        <p>
                            Many expats use ride apps for everyday movement
                            until they become familiar enough with the city to
                            combine Metro, autos and other options.
                        </p>
                    </details>

                    <details>
                        <summary>Auto-Rickshaws</summary>

                        <p>
                            Autos are one of the defining features of Delhi’s
                            streets. These three-wheelers are ideal for short
                            neighbourhood trips and quick distances where cars
                            would get stuck in traffic.
                        </p>

                        <p>
                            In busy markets or dense areas, autos can often move
                            faster than cars because they navigate small streets
                            more easily.
                        </p>

                        <p>
                            Drivers usually prefer agreeing on a fare before the
                            ride instead of using the meter. Once you learn the
                            typical pricing patterns, autos become a very
                            practical way to move around locally.
                        </p>
                    </details>

                    <details>
                        <summary>Private Drivers</summary>

                        <p>
                            Many long-term expats eventually hire a driver. It
                            might seem unusual at first, but in Delhi it can
                            remove a surprising amount of daily stress.
                        </p>

                        <p>
                            Traffic patterns are unpredictable and parking is
                            rarely simple. Having someone who understands the
                            city allows you to focus on where you're going
                            instead of how to get there.
                        </p>

                        <p>
                            Drivers are especially useful for commuting, airport
                            transfers or days when you need to visit multiple
                            places across the city.
                        </p>
                    </details>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- SAFETY PANEL -->

            <div class="guide-panel">
                <div class="panel-header">
                    <svg class="panel-icon" viewBox="0 0 64 64">
                        <circle cx="32" cy="32" r="26"></circle>
                        <path d="M32 18v28M20 32h24"></path>
                    </svg>

                    <div>
                        <h3>Safety Awareness</h3>
                        <p>
                            Understanding a few local dynamics helps avoid
                            common issues.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="accordion">
                    <details>
                        <summary>Common Tourist Scams</summary>

                        <p>
                            Delhi is generally safe, but like any large city
                            there are a few situations that catch newcomers off
                            guard.
                        </p>

                        <p>
                            One common example is drivers claiming a monument or
                            market is closed and suggesting an alternative
                            location. These places are often shops or travel
                            offices that pay commissions.
                        </p>

                        <p>
                            The easiest way to avoid this is simple: rely on
                            your own navigation and verify information
                            independently.
                        </p>
                    </details>

                    <details>
                        <summary>Night Travel</summary>

                        <p>
                            Delhi remains active late into the evening,
                            particularly in areas like Khan Market, Hauz Khas,
                            Connaught Place and parts of South Delhi.
                        </p>

                        <p>
                            Ride-hailing apps are usually the most comfortable
                            option for late travel. They provide route tracking
                            and remove the need to arrange transport in
                            unfamiliar areas.
                        </p>

                        <p>
                            Like most major cities, it’s best to stick to
                            well-lit streets and busy areas when exploring
                            somewhere new at night.
                        </p>
                    </details>

                    <details>
                        <summary>Digital Payments</summary>

                        <p>
                            India has moved rapidly toward digital payments and
                            Delhi reflects that change everywhere.
                        </p>

                        <p>
                            UPI payments — through apps like Google Pay, PhonePe
                            or Paytm — are accepted in cafés, taxis, markets and
                            even small neighbourhood shops.
                        </p>

                        <p>
                            For newcomers this quickly becomes the easiest way
                            to handle everyday transactions without worrying
                            about cash.
                        </p>
                    </details>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- LEAD GENERATION -->

            <div class="lead-panel">
                <h3>Learning Delhi Alone Takes Time</h3>

                <p>
                    Most newcomers spend months figuring out transport patterns,
                    local etiquette and neighbourhood logistics.
                </p>

                <p>
                    A local concierge can shorten that learning curve
                    dramatically and help you move through the city with
                    confidence from the start.
                </p>

                <a href="/services" class="btn"> Book a Local Consultation </a>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- CTA -->

    <CTA />

    <style>
        ================= HERO ================= */
        .hero {
            position: relative;
            overflow: hidden;
        } /* decorative ambient glow */
        .hero::before {
            content: "";
            position: absolute;
            width: 420px;
            height: 420px;
            top: -180px;
            right: -160px;
            background: radial-gradient(
                circle,
                rgba(238, 142, 67, 0.25) 0%,
                transparent 65%
            );
            filter: blur(40px);
            z-index: 0;
        }
        .hero::after {
            content: "";
            position: absolute;
            width: 420px;
            height: 420px;
            bottom: -200px;
            left: -160px;
            background: radial-gradient(
                circle,
                rgba(92, 204, 251, 0.25) 0%,
                transparent 65%
            );
            filter: blur(40px);
            z-index: 0;
        } /* hero layout */
        .hero-wrapper {
            display: grid;
            grid-template-columns: 1.2fr 0.8fr;
            gap: 4rem;
            align-items: center;
            position: relative;
            z-index: 2;
        } /* hero image */
        .main-img {
            width: 100%;
            border-radius: 22px;
            box-shadow: 0 30px 70px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.15);
            transform: rotate(-2deg);
            transition: 0.35s ease;
        }
        .main-img:hover {
            transform: rotate(0deg) scale(1.02);
        } /* responsive hero */
        @media (max-width: 1024px) {
            .hero-wrapper {
                grid-template-columns: 1fr;
                gap: 2.5rem;
            }
            .main-img {
                max-width: 600px;
                margin: auto;
                display: block;
            }
        } /* ================= GUIDE SECTION ================= */
        .guide-container {
            max-width: 900px;
            margin: auto;
        }
        .guide-title {
            font-size: 30px;
            margin-bottom: 10px;
        }
        .guide-intro {
            color: var(--text-secondary);
            margin-bottom: 40px;
        } /* ================= PANELS ================= */
        .guide-panel {
            margin-bottom: 40px;
            padding: 28px;
            border-radius: 20px;
            background: var(--bg-surface);
            border: 1px solid var(--border-soft);
            box-shadow:
                0 10px 30px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.06),
                inset 0 1px 0 rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.4);
            transition: 0.25s;
        }
        .guide-panel:hover {
            transform: translateY(-4px);
            box-shadow: 0 22px 55px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.12);
        } /* ================= PANEL HEADER ================= */
        .panel-header {
            display: flex;
            gap: 16px;
            align-items: flex-start;
            margin-bottom: 20px;
        }
        .panel-icon {
            width: 38px;
            height: 38px;
            stroke: var(--accent-blue);
            stroke-width: 2;
            fill: none;
            opacity: 0.8;
        } /* ================= ACCORDION ================= */
        .accordion details {
            border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-soft);
            padding: 16px 0;
        }
        .accordion summary {
            cursor: pointer;
            font-weight: 600;
        }
        .accordion p {
            margin-top: 8px;
            color: var(--text-secondary);
            max-width: 640px;
        } /* ================= LEAD PANEL ================= */
        .lead-panel {
            margin-top: 60px;
            padding: 36px;
            border-radius: 22px;
            text-align: center;
            background: var(--bg-surface);
            border: 1px solid var(--border-soft);
            box-shadow:
                0 10px 30px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.06),
                inset 0 1px 0 rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.4);
        }
        .lead-panel p {
            margin-bottom: 12px;
        }
    </style>
</BaseLayout>
